
# Hardware Components – Six-Wheel ROS 2 Rover

## 1. Main Computing Unit

### Raspberry Pi 5 (4GB)
- Acts as the main computing unit.
- Runs Ubuntu 22.04.
- Runs ROS 2 Humble.
- Receives movement commands from the laptop over Wi-Fi.
- Handles high-level robot control and sensor data processing.
- Provides the platform for future AI integration.

## 2. Motor Control Unit

### ESP32 Dev Kit
- Acts as the low-level motor controller.
- Receives control commands from Raspberry Pi.
- Generates motor direction and PWM signals.
- Controls six individual N20 motors through three motor drivers.

### TB6612FNG Motor Driver
Quantity: 3

- Each driver controls two DC motors.
- Provides bidirectional motor control.
- Supports PWM-based speed control.
- Allows independent control of six motors using three drivers.

## 3. Drive System

### N20 Geared DC Motors
Quantity: 6

- Provides the rover's driving force.
- Each wheel is driven by an individual motor.
- Supports individual wheel movement and speed control.

### Mechanical Suspension
Type: Rocker-Bogie

- Six-wheel mechanical arrangement.
- Designed for improved wheel contact on uneven terrain.
- Provides a platform for rough-terrain mobility.

## 4. Power System

### 2S Li-ion Battery
- Nominal voltage: 7.4 V.
- Supplies the rover's electrical power system.
- Power distribution and voltage regulation must be designed for the motors, Raspberry Pi and ESP32.

## 5. Sensor System

### MPU6050
- Measures acceleration and angular velocity.
- Provides motion and orientation-related data.
- Can support future terrain-condition analysis.

### Ultrasonic Sensor
- Measures distance to nearby objects.
- Can support obstacle detection.

### Camera
- Provides visual information from the rover.
- Intended for future computer vision and AI applications.

### Additional Sensors
- Additional sensor details will be documented after final component selection.

## 6. Communication System

### Laptop to Raspberry Pi
- Communication: Wi-Fi.
- Purpose: Remote operation and teleoperation.

### Raspberry Pi to ESP32
- Communication: Wi-Fi.
- Purpose: Transfer of motor-control commands.

## 7. Software Platform

| Platform | Technology |
|---|---|
| Main computer | Raspberry Pi 5 |
